      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70736,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70737,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is centred in the rete testis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70738,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with a mass and/or pain. The tumour can be associated with hydrocoele {17853037}. Local spread and metastasis to para-aortic and iliac lymph nodes are common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70739,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is exceedingly rare. It occurs in a wide age range, although most reported cases are in adults.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70740,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70741,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70742,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are centred in the testicular hilum and have solid and cystic cut surfaces {30676333}. They are typically large, with reported diameters of 20&ndash;90&nbsp;mm {32619438}; extension to spermatic cord and overlying skin with satellite nodules is common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70743,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p>Histologically, the tumours show intrarete and invasive growth, with a range of patterns such as papillary, solid, glandular, cribriform, and glomeruloid {30676333}. Tumour cells are cuboidal to columnar with nuclear pseudostratification and noticeable cytological atypia. The cytoplasm varies from eosinophilic to clear. Desmoplasia and necrosis are common. Evidence of a transition from normal to neoplastic rete epithelium is a useful diagnostic clue if present; even so, large masses can obliterate the normal anatomy and this transition is not documentable. Immunohistochemistry is positive for CK7, AE1/AE3, EMA, vimentin, PAX8, and BerEP4; there are no specific lineage-associated (rete epithelium) markers {30676333}. The differential diagnosis includes mesothelioma, ovarian-type tumours, metastatic adenocarcinoma, epididymal carcinoma, and malignant Sertoli cell tumour. Supportive immunohistochemistry ruling out other lineage differentiation tumours such as metastatic adenocarcinoma, germ cell tumours, Sertoli cell tumour, or mesothelioma can help in the accurate diagnosis of rete testis carcinoma {30676333}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-15T17:43:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70744,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 173,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No published reports</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
